/-!
# The stackification of the discrete pseudofunctor of a separated presheaf

Let `P` be a presheaf of types on a category `C` with pullbacks and a Grothendieck topology `J`.
The fibres `Obj J (ofPresheaf P) U` of the stackification construction, applied to the discrete
pseudofunctor of `P`, consist of descent data along `w`-small covering families of `U`. Such a
descent datum `A` is a family of elements `A.elem i` of `P` over the members of the covering
family which agree on overlaps (`Obj.map_elem_eq`); these are read off with
`Pseudofunctor.ofPresheaf.descentDataEquiv`, and conversely such a family defines a descent datum
through `Obj.ofDescentData` and the inverse of that equivalence (`Obj.elem_ofDescentData`). A
morphism `A ⟶ B` exists exactly when the elements of `A` and of `B` agree on overlaps
(`Obj.nonempty_hom_iff`); there is at most one (`Obj.instSubsingletonHom`).

A descent datum defines a matching family of `P` on the covering sieve generated by its
covering family, hence an element `Obj.toPlusObj A` of Mathlib's plus construction
`(J.plusObj P).obj (op U)`. When `P` is separated, that is, when the discrete pseudofunctor is a
prestack (`Pseudofunctor.isPrestack_ofPresheaf_iff`), the fibre `Obj J (ofPresheaf P) U` is a
thin category, and `Obj.toPlusObj` identifies its isomorphism classes with
`(J.plusObj P).obj (op U)` provided every covering sieve of `J` contains a covering sieve
generated by a `w`-small family (`Obj.isoClassesEquivPlusObj`); this holds for `w = max u v`
(Mathlib's `Sieve.exists_eq_ofArrows`). For separated `P`, the plus construction `J.plusObj P` is
already a sheaf (Mathlib's `GrothendieckTopology.Plus.isSheaf_of_sep`), so the fibres are, up to
isomorphism, the sections of the sheafification of `P`, and its discrete pseudofunctor is a stack
(`TauCeti.Stack.isStack_ofPresheaf_plusObj`).

The elements `toPlusObj` are compatible with pullbacks of descent data (`Obj.toPlusObj_pullObj`)
and send the descent datum along the identity of `U` given by an element of `P` to its image under
`J.toPlus P` (`Obj.toPlusObj_toObjFunctor_obj`). Hence they form a strong transformation
`TauCeti.Stack.stackificationDiscreteHom` from `stackification J (ofPresheaf P)` to the discrete
pseudofunctor of `J.plusObj P`. Provided every covering sieve of `J` contains a covering sieve
generated by a `w`-small family (for instance when `w = max u v`), its components are
equivalences of categories, so it is an equivalence of pseudofunctors
(`TauCeti.Stack.stackificationDiscreteEquiv`, Stacks, Section 02ZM).
Composed with the unit `TauCeti.Stack.toStackification`, it is the strong transformation induced
by `J.toPlus P` (`TauCeti.Stack.toStackificationCompStackificationDiscreteHomIso`). So for a
separated presheaf, under this condition on covering sieves, the stackification of its discrete
pseudofunctor is the discrete stack of its sheafification, with the unit of the stackification
corresponding to the unit of the sheafification.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Stack.Stackification.Obj.elem`: the elements of `P` underlying a descent datum.
* `TauCeti.Stack.Stackification.Obj.toPlusObj`: the element of the plus construction given by a
  descent datum.
* `TauCeti.Stack.Stackification.Obj.isoClassesEquivPlusObj`: for separated `P`, isomorphism
  classes of descent data are elements of the plus construction, when every covering sieve
  contains a covering sieve generated by a `w`-small family.
* `TauCeti.Stack.Stackification.Obj.toPlusObjFunctor`: `toPlusObj` as a functor to the discrete
  category on the sections of the plus construction, an equivalence of categories when every
  covering sieve contains a covering sieve generated by a `w`-small family
  (`Obj.isEquivalence_toPlusObjFunctor`).
* `TauCeti.Stack.stackificationDiscreteEquiv`: for separated `P`, when every covering sieve
  contains a covering sieve generated by a `w`-small family, the stackification of the discrete
  pseudofunctor of `P` is equivalent to the discrete pseudofunctor of `J.plusObj P`.
* `TauCeti.Stack.toStackificationCompStackificationDiscreteHomIso`: this equivalence is
  compatible with the unit of the stackification and with `J.toPlus P`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Section 02ZM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02ZM)
-/

public section

noncomputable section

universe w w' w'' v u

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite Bicategory Pseudofunctor Pseudofunctor.ofPresheaf
  GrothendieckTopology

namespace TauCeti.Stack.Stackification.Obj

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {U : C}

section

variable {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w''}

/-- The element of `P` over the `i`-th member of the covering family of a descent datum for the
discrete pseudofunctor of `P`. -/
def elem (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) (i : A.ι) : P.obj (op (A.X i)) :=
  (descentDataEquiv A.f A.D).val i

/-- The elements underlying a descent datum for the discrete pseudofunctor agree on overlaps. -/
lemma map_elem_eq (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) ⦃T : C⦄ ⦃i i' : A.ι⦄ (a : T ⟶ A.X i)
    (a' : T ⟶ A.X i') (h : a ≫ A.f i = a' ≫ A.f i') :
    P.map a.op (A.elem i) = P.map a'.op (A.elem i') :=
  (descentDataEquiv A.f A.D).property _ _ _ a a' h

/-- The element of `P` underlying a descent datum over the `i`-th member of its covering family is
the element given by its `i`-th object. -/
lemma elem_def (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) (i : A.ι) :
    A.elem i = objEquiv _ (A.D.obj i) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The elements underlying a descent datum along a fixed covering family are given by its
objects. -/
@[simp]
lemma elem_ofDescentData {ι : Type w} {X : ι → C} (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U)
    (hf : Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U) (D : (ofPresheaf.{w'} P).DescentData f) (i : ι) :
    (ofDescentData f hf D).elem i = objEquiv _ (D.obj i) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The matching family of `P` on the cover generated by the covering family of a descent datum
for the discrete pseudofunctor, given by its underlying elements. -/
def meq (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) : Meq P A.cover :=
  ⟨fun I ↦
    have hI : Sieve.ofArrows A.X A.f I.f := A.coe_cover ▸ I.hf
    P.map (Sieve.ofArrows.h hI).op (A.elem (Sieve.ofArrows.i hI)),
    fun I ↦ by
      simp only [← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp]
      exact A.map_elem_eq _ _ (by simpa only [Category.assoc, Sieve.ofArrows.fac] using I.r.w)⟩

/-- The matching family of a descent datum is computed by any factorization through its covering
family. -/
lemma meq_apply (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) (I : A.cover.Arrow) {i : A.ι}
    (a : I.Y ⟶ A.X i) (h : a ≫ A.f i = I.f) : A.meq I = P.map a.op (A.elem i) :=
  A.map_elem_eq _ _ (by rw [Sieve.ofArrows.fac, h])

variable [HasPullbacks C]

/-- There is at most one morphism between descent data for the discrete pseudofunctor. -/
instance instSubsingletonHom (A B : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) : Subsingleton (Hom A B) :=
  ⟨fun _ _ ↦ Hom.ext (funext fun _ ↦ funext fun _ ↦ Subsingleton.elim _ _)⟩

/-- A morphism between descent data for the discrete pseudofunctor exists exactly when their
underlying elements agree on overlaps. -/
lemma nonempty_hom_iff (A B : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) :
    Nonempty (Hom A B) ↔ ∀ ⦃T : C⦄ ⦃i : A.ι⦄ ⦃j : B.ι⦄ (a : T ⟶ A.X i) (b : T ⟶ B.X j),
      a ≫ A.f i = b ≫ B.f j → P.map a.op (A.elem i) = P.map b.op (B.elem j) := by
  refine ⟨fun ⟨φ⟩ T i j a b w ↦ eq_of_hom (X := op T) (φ.app a b w), fun h ↦ ⟨?_⟩⟩
  exact Hom.ofApp (fun T i j a b w ↦ homMk (X := op T) (h a b w))
    (fun _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ↦ Subsingleton.elim _ _)
    (fun _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ↦ Subsingleton.elim _ _)

end

variable {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (max w u v)}

/-- The element of the plus construction `(J.plusObj P).obj (op U)` given by a descent datum for
the discrete pseudofunctor of `P`: the class of its matching family. -/
def toPlusObj (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) : (J.plusObj P).obj (op U) :=
  Plus.mk A.meq

/-- `toPlusObj A` is the class of the matching family of `A` in the plus construction. -/
lemma toPlusObj_def (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) : A.toPlusObj = Plus.mk A.meq :=
  (rfl)

/-- Every element of the plus construction is given by a descent datum along a `w`-small covering
family, provided every covering sieve contains a covering sieve generated by a `w`-small
family. -/
theorem toPlusObj_surjective
    (hJ : ∀ S ∈ J U, ∃ (ι : Type w) (X : ι → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ Sieve.ofArrows X f ≤ S) :
    Function.Surjective fun A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U ↦ A.toPlusObj := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨S, y, rfl⟩ := Plus.exists_rep (J := J) (P := P) (X := U) x
  obtain ⟨ι, X, f, hf, hle⟩ := hJ S S.property
  have hy (i : ι) : S (f i) := hle _ (Sieve.ofArrows_mk _ _ i)
  -- `y` restricts along `a : T ⟶ X i` to its value at `a ≫ f i`.
  have key ⦃T : C⦄ (i : ι) (a : T ⟶ X i) :
      P.map a.op (y ⟨X i, f i, hy i⟩) = y ⟨T, a ≫ f i, S.val.downward_closed (hy i) a⟩ := by
    have h : P.map (𝟙 T).op (y ⟨T, a ≫ f i, S.val.downward_closed (hy i) a⟩) =
        P.map a.op (y ⟨X i, f i, hy i⟩) :=
      y.property (.mk' (Cover.Arrow.precompRelation ⟨X i, f i, hy i⟩ a))
    simpa using h.symm
  let A := ofDescentData.{w} (J := J) (F := ofPresheaf.{w'} P) f hf
    ((descentDataEquiv f).symm ⟨fun i ↦ y ⟨X i, f i, hy i⟩, fun i i' T a a' h ↦ by
      rw [key, key]
      exact Meq.congr_apply y h _⟩)
  refine ⟨A, (Plus.eq_mk_iff_exists _ _).2 ⟨A.cover, 𝟙 _,
    homOfLE (Subtype.coe_le_coe.1 (by rw [coe_cover]; exact hle)), Meq.ext _ _ fun I ↦ ?_⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨i, a, ha⟩ := Sieve.ofArrows.exists (A.coe_cover ▸ I.hf)
  simp only [Meq.refine_apply]
  rw [meq_apply A I a ha.symm]
  exact (key i a).trans (Meq.congr_apply y ha.symm _)

variable [HasPullbacks C]

/-- The elements underlying the pullback of a descent datum along `q : V ⟶ U` are the restrictions
of those of the descent datum along the projections `A.X i ×_U V ⟶ A.X i`. -/
lemma elem_pullObj {V : C} (q : V ⟶ U) (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) (i : A.ι) :
    (pullObj q A).elem i = P.map (pullback.fst (A.f i) q).op (A.elem i) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The element of the plus construction given by the pullback of a descent datum along
`q : V ⟶ U` is the restriction along `q` of the element given by the descent datum. -/
@[simp]
lemma toPlusObj_pullObj {V : C} (q : V ⟶ U) (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) :
    (pullObj q A).toPlusObj = (J.plusObj P).map q.op A.toPlusObj := by
  rw [toPlusObj, toPlusObj, Plus.res_mk_eq_mk_pullback, Plus.eq_mk_iff_exists]
  refine ⟨(pullObj q A).cover, 𝟙 _, homOfLE fun T g hg ↦ ?_, Meq.ext _ _ fun I ↦ ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨i, a, rfl⟩ := Sieve.ofArrows.exists ((pullObj q A).coe_cover ▸ hg)
    rw [pullback_obj, Cover.coe_pullback, coe_cover]
    exact (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ _).2
      ⟨i, a ≫ pullback.fst (A.f i) q, by simp [pullback.condition]⟩
  · obtain ⟨i, a, ha⟩ := Sieve.ofArrows.exists ((pullObj q A).coe_cover ▸ I.hf)
    rw [Meq.refine_apply, Meq.refine_apply, meq_apply _ I a ha.symm, Meq.pullback_apply,
      meq_apply A _ (a ≫ pullback.fst (A.f i) q) (by simp [ha, pullback.condition]),
      elem_pullObj, op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply]

/-- Two descent data for the discrete pseudofunctor of a separated presheaf define the same
element of the plus construction exactly when there is a morphism between them. -/
theorem toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff (hP : Presieve.IsSeparated J P)
    (A B : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) :
    A.toPlusObj = B.toPlusObj ↔ Nonempty (Hom A B) := by
  rw [toPlusObj, toPlusObj, Plus.eq_mk_iff_exists, nonempty_hom_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨W, h₁, h₂, e⟩ T i j a b w
    refine (hP _ (J.pullback_stable (a ≫ A.f i) W.property)).ext fun T' g hg ↦ ?_
    have := congr_arg (fun x : Meq P W ↦ x ⟨T', g ≫ a ≫ A.f i, hg⟩) e
    simp only [Meq.refine_apply] at this
    rw [meq_apply A _ (g ≫ a) (Category.assoc _ _ _),
      meq_apply B _ (g ≫ b) (by simp [w])] at this
    simpa only [op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply] using this
  · intro h
    refine ⟨A.cover ⊓ B.cover, homOfLE inf_le_left, homOfLE inf_le_right,
      Meq.ext _ _ fun I ↦ ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨i, a, ha⟩ := Sieve.ofArrows.exists (A.coe_cover ▸ inf_le_left (b := B.cover) _ I.hf)
    obtain ⟨j, b, hb⟩ := Sieve.ofArrows.exists (B.coe_cover ▸ inf_le_right (a := A.cover) _ I.hf)
    rw [Meq.refine_apply, Meq.refine_apply, meq_apply A _ a ha.symm, meq_apply B _ b hb.symm]
    exact h a b (ha.symm.trans hb)

variable [(ofPresheaf.{w'} P).IsPrestack J]

/-- For a separated presheaf `P`, there is at most one morphism between two descent data for the
discrete pseudofunctor of `P`. -/
instance instIsThin : Quiver.IsThin (Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) :=
  fun A B ↦ inferInstanceAs (Subsingleton (Hom A B))

/-- For a separated presheaf `P`, two descent data for the discrete pseudofunctor of `P` are
isomorphic exactly when they define the same element of the plus construction. -/
theorem toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff_isIsomorphic (A B : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) :
    A.toPlusObj = B.toPlusObj ↔ IsIsomorphic A B := by
  have hP := (isPrestack_ofPresheaf_iff P J).1 inferInstance
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun ⟨e⟩ ↦ (toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff hP A B).2 ⟨e.hom⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨φ⟩ := (toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff hP A B).1 h
  obtain ⟨ψ⟩ := (toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff hP B A).1 h.symm
  exact ⟨⟨φ, ψ, Subsingleton.elim _ _, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩⟩

/-- For a separated presheaf `P`, isomorphism classes of descent data along `w`-small covering
families for the discrete pseudofunctor of `P` are the elements of the plus construction
`(J.plusObj P).obj (op U)`, provided every covering sieve contains a covering sieve generated by a
`w`-small family. -/
def isoClassesEquivPlusObj
    (hJ : ∀ S ∈ J U, ∃ (ι : Type w) (X : ι → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ Sieve.ofArrows X f ≤ S) :
    Quotient (isIsomorphicSetoid (Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U)) ≃
      (J.plusObj P).obj (op U) :=
  Equiv.ofBijective
    (Quotient.lift toPlusObj fun A B h ↦ (toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff_isIsomorphic A B).2 h)
    ⟨fun a b ↦ Quotient.inductionOn₂ a b fun A B h ↦
        Quotient.sound ((toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff_isIsomorphic A B).1 h),
      fun x ↦ (toPlusObj_surjective hJ x).elim fun A h ↦ ⟨⟦A⟧, h⟩⟩

/-- `isoClassesEquivPlusObj` sends the class of a descent datum to its element of the plus
construction. -/
@[simp]
lemma isoClassesEquivPlusObj_mk
    (hJ : ∀ S ∈ J U, ∃ (ι : Type w) (X : ι → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ Sieve.ofArrows X f ≤ S)
    (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) :
    isoClassesEquivPlusObj hJ ⟦A⟧ = A.toPlusObj :=
  (rfl)

/-- The element of the plus construction given by the descent datum along the identity of `U`
attached to an object `M` of the fibre over `U`, that is, to the element `objEquiv _ M` of `P`
over `U`, is the image of this element under `J.toPlus P`. -/
lemma toPlusObj_toObjFunctor_obj (M : (ofPresheaf.{w'} P).obj (.mk (op U))) :
    ((toObjFunctor.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U).obj M).toPlusObj =
      (J.toPlus P).app (op U) (objEquiv _ M) := by
  rw [toPlusObj, Plus.toPlus_mk ((toObjFunctor.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U).obj M).cover]
  congr 1
  refine Meq.ext _ _ fun I ↦ ?_
  rw [meq_apply _ I (i := PUnit.unit) I.f (Category.comp_id _), Meq.mk_apply]
  -- The object of the descent datum `(toObjFunctor J _ U).obj M` is the pullback of `M` along
  -- `𝟙 U` by definition of `Pseudofunctor.toDescentData`, so `objEquiv_map_toFunctor_obj`
  -- applies to it by unification.
  exact congrArg (P.map I.f.op) ((objEquiv_map_toFunctor_obj (𝟙 U).op.toLoc M).trans (by simp))

variable (J P) in
/-- The functor from descent data for the discrete pseudofunctor of a separated presheaf `P`
along `w`-small covering families of `U` to the discrete category on the sections over `U` of the
plus construction `J.plusObj P`, sending a descent datum to its element `toPlusObj`. -/
def toPlusObjFunctor (U : C) :
    Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U ⥤ (ofPresheaf.{w''} (J.plusObj P)).obj (.mk (op U)) where
  obj A := (objEquiv _).symm A.toPlusObj
  map {A B} φ := homMk (X := op U)
    ((toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff ((isPrestack_ofPresheaf_iff P J).1 inferInstance) A B).2 ⟨φ⟩)
  map_id _ := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  map_comp _ _ := Subsingleton.elim _ _

/-- The functor `toPlusObjFunctor` sends a descent datum to its element of the plus
construction. -/
@[simp]
lemma objEquiv_toPlusObjFunctor_obj (A : Obj.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P) U) :
    objEquiv (op U) ((toPlusObjFunctor.{w, w', w''} J P U).obj A) = A.toPlusObj :=
  (rfl)

/-- The functor `toPlusObjFunctor` is full: descent data with the same element of the plus
construction are related by a morphism. -/
instance full_toPlusObjFunctor : (toPlusObjFunctor.{w, w', w''} J P U).Full :=
  ⟨fun {A B} φ ↦ ⟨((toPlusObj_eq_toPlusObj_iff ((isPrestack_ofPresheaf_iff P J).1 inferInstance)
    A B).1 (eq_of_hom (X := op U) φ)).some, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩⟩

/-- The functor `toPlusObjFunctor` is essentially surjective, provided every covering sieve of `U`
contains a covering sieve generated by a `w`-small family. -/
lemma essSurj_toPlusObjFunctor
    (hJ : ∀ S ∈ J U, ∃ (ι : Type w) (X : ι → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ Sieve.ofArrows X f ≤ S) :
    (toPlusObjFunctor.{w, w', w''} J P U).EssSurj :=
  ⟨fun x ↦ (toPlusObj_surjective hJ (objEquiv _ x)).elim fun A h ↦ ⟨A, ⟨isoMk h⟩⟩⟩

/-- The functor `toPlusObjFunctor` is an equivalence of categories, provided every covering sieve
of `U` contains a covering sieve generated by a `w`-small family. -/
lemma isEquivalence_toPlusObjFunctor
    (hJ : ∀ S ∈ J U, ∃ (ι : Type w) (X : ι → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ Sieve.ofArrows X f ≤ S) :
    (toPlusObjFunctor.{w, w', w''} J P U).IsEquivalence :=
  have := essSurj_toPlusObjFunctor.{w, w', w''} (P := P) hJ
  { }

end TauCeti.Stack.Stackification.Obj

namespace TauCeti.Stack

open Stackification Obj
open scoped StrongTrans

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) [HasPullbacks C]
  (P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (max w u v))

omit [HasPullbacks C] in
/-- For a separated presheaf `P`, the plus construction `J.plusObj P` is a sheaf, so its discrete
pseudofunctor is a stack. -/
lemma isStack_ofPresheaf_plusObj (hP : Presieve.IsSeparated J P) :
    (ofPresheaf.{w'} (J.plusObj P)).IsStack J :=
  isStack_ofPresheaf J
    ⟨J.plusObj P, Plus.isSheaf_of_sep P fun _ S _ _ h ↦
      (hP S S.condition).ext fun _ f hf ↦ h ⟨_, f, hf⟩⟩

section

variable [(ofPresheaf.{w'} P).IsPrestack J]

/-- The strong transformation from the stackification of the discrete pseudofunctor of a
separated presheaf `P` to the discrete pseudofunctor of the plus construction `J.plusObj P`,
whose component over `U` sends a descent datum to its element of `(J.plusObj P).obj (op U)`
(`Stackification.Obj.toPlusObjFunctor`). -/
def stackificationDiscreteHom :
    StrongTrans (stackification.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P))
      (ofPresheaf.{max (w + 1) w'} (J.plusObj P)) where
  app a := (toPlusObjFunctor J P a.as.unop).toCatHom
  -- The naturality isomorphisms compare the elements `toPlusObj` of a pulled back descent datum
  -- and the restriction of `toPlusObj`; these are the objects of the composite functors only
  -- after unfolding them, so `toPlusObj_pullObj` is applied by `exact`. The coherence conditions
  -- hold because the fibres of the target are discrete.
  naturality f := Cat.Hom.isoMk (NatIso.ofComponents
    (fun A ↦ isoMk (by exact toPlusObj_pullObj f.as.unop A)) (fun _ ↦ Subsingleton.elim _ _))
  naturality_naturality _ := by ext; exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
  naturality_id _ := by ext; exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
  naturality_comp _ _ := by ext; exact Subsingleton.elim _ _

/-- The component of `stackificationDiscreteHom` over `U` is `toPlusObjFunctor`. -/
@[simp]
lemma stackificationDiscreteHom_app_toFunctor (a : LocallyDiscrete Cᵒᵖ) :
    ((stackificationDiscreteHom.{w, w'} J P).app a).toFunctor = toPlusObjFunctor J P a.as.unop :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The stackification of the discrete pseudofunctor of a separated presheaf** (Stacks,
Section 02ZM): if every covering sieve of `J` contains a covering sieve generated by a family
indexed by a type in `Type w`, then `stackificationDiscreteHom` is an equivalence between the
stackification of the discrete pseudofunctor of a separated presheaf `P` and the discrete
pseudofunctor of the sheaf `J.plusObj P`, the sheafification of `P`. -/
def stackificationDiscreteEquiv
    (hJ : ∀ ⦃U : C⦄, ∀ R ∈ J U, ∃ (ι : Type w) (X : ι → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ Sieve.ofArrows X f ≤ R) :
    Bicategory.Equivalence (stackification.{w} J (ofPresheaf.{w'} P))
      (ofPresheaf.{max (w + 1) w'} (J.plusObj P)) :=
  have (a : LocallyDiscrete Cᵒᵖ) :
      ((stackificationDiscreteHom.{w, w'} J P).app a).toFunctor.IsEquivalence :=
    isEquivalence_toPlusObjFunctor (fun R hR ↦ hJ R hR)
  (stackificationDiscreteHom J P).equivalenceOfIsEquivalence

/-- The forward strong transformation of `stackificationDiscreteEquiv` is
`stackificationDiscreteHom`. -/
@[simp]
lemma stackificationDiscreteEquiv_hom
    (hJ : ∀ ⦃U : C⦄, ∀ R ∈ J U, ∃ (ι : Type w) (X : ι → C) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows X f ∈ J U ∧ Sieve.ofArrows X f ≤ R) :
    (stackificationDiscreteEquiv.{w, w'} J P hJ).hom = stackificationDiscreteHom J P :=
  (rfl)

end

variable [(ofPresheaf.{max (w + 1) w'} P).IsPrestack J]

attribute [local instance] uliftCategory

/-- The unit of the stackification followed by `stackificationDiscreteHom` is the strong
transformation induced by the morphism `J.toPlus P : P ⟶ J.plusObj P` to the plus construction. -/
def toStackificationCompStackificationDiscreteHomIso :
    Iso (C := ofPresheaf.{max (w + 1) w'} P ⟶ ofPresheaf.{max (w + 1) w'} (J.plusObj P))
      ((toStackification.{w, max u v, max (w + 1) w'} J (ofPresheaf.{max (w + 1) w'} P)).vcomp
        (stackificationDiscreteHom.{w, max (w + 1) w'} J P))
      (ofPresheafMap.{max (w + 1) w'} (J.toPlus P)) :=
  -- As for `stackificationDiscreteHom`, the objects of the composite functors are those of
  -- `toPlusObj_toObjFunctor_obj` only after unfolding, and the fibres of the target are discrete.
  StrongTrans.isoMk
    (fun a ↦ Cat.Hom.isoMk (NatIso.ofComponents
      (fun M ↦ isoMk (by exact toPlusObj_toObjFunctor_obj M))
      (fun _ ↦ Subsingleton.elim (α := (_ : ULift (Discrete _)) ⟶ _) _ _)))
    (fun _ ↦ by ext; exact Subsingleton.elim _ _)

end TauCeti.Stack

